# {{.Command}}

Summarize TLEGO position JSON v1 from stdin. This project uses only Go's standard library and works independently of TLEGO.

## Build and test

```bash
go test ./...
go build -o {{.Command}} .
./{{.Command}} --help
```

On Windows use `go build -o {{.Command}}.exe .` and run `.\{{.Command}}.exe --help`.

## Install and run through TLEGO

```bash
go install .
```

Put `go env GOBIN`, or `go env GOPATH` followed by `/bin` when GOBIN is empty, on your PATH. On Windows use the corresponding `bin` directory and an `.exe` executable.

```bash
tlego plugin list
tlego {{.Name}} --help
tlego predict --time 2026-10-24T05:01:11Z --format json 25544 | tlego {{.Name}}
```

For an offline pipeline, replace `25544` with `--file /absolute/path/to/satellite.tle`. You can also run `{{.Command}} < position.json` directly.

## Customize

Edit `summarize` in `main.go`. Keep stdout for results, stderr for errors and diagnostics, and return a nonzero status on failure. Validate the schema major and record kind before using fields. Ignore unfamiliar fields and warning codes within a compatible schema major. Tests should cover malformed input, incompatible versions and useful output.

The host passes arguments and streams directly. It supplies `TLEGO_HOST_VERSION` and `TLEGO_EXTENSION_VERSION`. No host imports or Go SDK are required. See TLEGO's `docs/extensions.md` for the full protocol and schema.
